=== Text #12 ===
> [This] pet friendly hotel offers guests a[ del]uxe breakfast each morning, free Wi-Fi, a business center, laundry facilities, and meeting space. This hotel is 15 minutes to the Atlanta Speedway, 3 miles to the Renaissance Festival.
Standard rooms feature free wireless internet access, cable TV with extra stations, free local calls, coffeemaker, microwave, mini-fridge and iron and board.
Guests will enjoy a deluxe breakfast each morning, as well as free Wi-Fi, use of the business center, laundry facilities, and a meeting space is available. Pets are welcome with additional charges.
Meeting space that can accommodate up to 60 people theater style and 30 people round table style are available on-site.[][][][]

=== Text #13 ===
> [You] can't say[ it]'s not[ thoroughly] deserved. Two impressive achievements by Claudio Marchis[io] rightly called for a standing ovation from the Juventus Stadium faithful before the match against Cagliari[.] And Il Princip[ino] duly collected two awards for his efforts following the pre-match warm-up[.]
First there was a commemorative plaque for his 300th Bianconeri appearance – which came against Fiorentina last week – handed to him[ by president Andrea] Ag[nell]i[.]
Then it was time for[ J]-Member Martina Divis to hand him the MVP of the Month Powered By Hanwha award for April on behalf of the Juventus Membership community[.
]A memorable night for Marchis[io] and an unforgettable[ one] for Martina, who got to meet one of her heroes while soaking up the[ pre]-match atmosphere on the hallowed J-Stadium turf[.
]Next time you could be the lucky J-Member doing the honours! You just need to go to the ON THE PITCH > Fixtures and Results section and vote for your man of the match after every game.
If you haven't joined the JuventusMembership family yet, don't delay: do it today! For more details, see here. #WeAreOne![]

